msgstr "この地形ではどのユニットも防御態勢をとれません。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:214 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:214
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:309 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:317
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:316 data/alien/terrain.ruleset:505
#: data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:307
msgid "Ocean"
msgstr "海"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:255 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:255
msgid "Oceans cover much of the world."
msgstr "海は世界の大部分を覆っています。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:257
msgid ""
"In cities built on the coast, stored food and work towards the current "
"project are at risk from piracy, unless there is any kind of Barracks in the "
"city."
msgstr ""
"海岸に建設された都市では、都市に何らかの兵舎がない限り、蓄えられた食料と現在"
"の生産に費やした作業が海賊に奪われる危険があります。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:264
msgid "Arctic"
msgstr "極地"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:305
msgid ""
"Arctic tiles are found only in the most northerly or southerly reaches of "
"the world.  They are very cold, and hence difficult to work with."
msgstr ""
"極地のタイルは世界の最北端または最南端にのみ存在します。非常に寒いため、作業"
"が困難です。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:312 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:308
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:462 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:470
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:469 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:454
msgid "Desert"
msgstr "砂漠"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:354 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:351
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:508 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:516
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:515 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:498
msgid ""
"Deserts are regions of extreme dryness, making agriculture and trade very "
"difficult."
msgstr "砂漠は極度に乾燥した地域であり、農業や交易が非常に困難です。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:360 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:357
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:516 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:530
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:529 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:506
msgid "Forest"
msgstr "森"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:404 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:401
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:563 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:577
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:576 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:551
msgid "Forests are densely wooded, making agriculture somewhat problematic."
msgstr "森は木々が密生しているため、農業にはやや問題があります。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:410 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:407
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:569 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:583
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:582 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:557
msgid "Grassland"
msgstr "草原"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:452 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:449
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:614 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:628
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:627 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:600
msgid "Grasslands afford exceptional agricultural opportunities."
msgstr "草原は農業に非常に適しています。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:457 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:454
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:619 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:633
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:632 data/alien/terrain.ruleset:410
#: data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:605
msgid "Hills"
msgstr "丘"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:499 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:496
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:664 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:678
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:677 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:648
msgid ""
"In addition to being amenable to agriculture, Hills are frequently rich in "
"resources."
msgstr "丘は農業に適しているうえ、資源も豊富なことが多くあります。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:502
msgid ""
"A city built in or next to hills is at risk of earthquakes, which can "
"destroy buildings in that city. There is no technology or improvement which "
"can prevent this disaster."
msgstr ""
"丘の上または隣に建設された都市は地震の危険があり、都市施設が破壊されることが"
"あります。この災害を防ぐ科学技術や都市施設はありません。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:509 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:502
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:670 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:687
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:686 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:654
msgid "Jungle"
msgstr "ジャングル"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:550 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:545
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:716 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:698
msgid "Jungles are densely overgrown, making agriculture somewhat problematic."
msgstr "ジャングルは植物が密生しているため、農業にはやや問題があります。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:556 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:551
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:722 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:740
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:739 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:704
msgid "Mountains"
msgstr "山"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:596 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:592
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:766 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:784
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:783 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:746
msgid ""
"Mountains are regions of extreme altitude, making agriculture and trade very "
"difficult."
msgstr "山は極めて標高の高い地域であり、農業や交易が非常に困難です。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:599
msgid ""
"Cities built in or next to mountains are at risk from volcanic activity. A "
"Temple in the city instils sufficient respect for the forces of nature to "
"prevent population loss."
msgstr ""
"山の上または隣に建設された都市は火山活動の危険があります。都市に寺院があれ"
"ば、自然の力に対する十分な敬意が育まれ、人口減少を防げます。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:606 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:598
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:772 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:795
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:794 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:752
msgid "Plains"
msgstr "平野"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:648 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:641
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:817 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:840
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:839 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:795
msgid ""
"Plains are very broad, sparse regions, which makes trade slightly "
"inconvenient."
msgstr "平野は非常に広く人のまばらな地域であり、交易がやや不便です。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:654 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:647
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:823 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:846
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:845 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:801
msgid "Swamp"
msgstr "湿地"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:697 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:691
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:870 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:846
msgid ""
"Swamps suffer from an over-abundance of water, making agriculture somewhat "
"problematic."
msgstr "湿地は水が多すぎるため、農業にはやや問題があります。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:703 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:697
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:876 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:900
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:899 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:852
msgid "Tundra"
msgstr "ツンドラ"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:744 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:738
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:920 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:944
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:943 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:894
msgid ""
"Tundra are broad, cold regions, fit for some agriculture and little else."
msgstr ""
"ツンドラは広大で寒冷な地域であり、多少の農業には適していますが、それ以外には"
"ほとんど適しません。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:835
msgid "?gui_type:Build Fortress"
msgstr "要塞を建設"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:838
msgid "?gui_type:Build None"
msgstr "何も建設しない"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:966 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1037
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1221 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:1245
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:1244 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1195
#: tools/manual/manual_terrain.c:51
msgid "Irrigation"
msgstr "灌漑"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:981 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1053
msgid ""
"Building an irrigation system on a suitable tile causes it to produce one "
"extra food each turn. This requires a nearby source of water: an ocean or "
"river tile, or another tile with an irrigation system, must share an edge "
"(not just a corner) with the target tile. However, once irrigated, land "
"remains so even if the water source is removed."
msgstr ""
"適したタイルに灌漑施設を建設すると、そのタイルは毎ターン食料を1多く産出しま"
"す。これには近くに水源が必要です。海や川のタイル、または灌漑施設のある他のタ"
"イルが、対象タイルと (角だけでなく) 辺を共有している必要があります。ただし、"
"一度灌漑された土地は、水源がなくなっても灌漑されたままです。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:988 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1060
msgid "Building irrigation on a tile with a mine will destroy it."
msgstr "鉱山のあるタイルに灌漑を建設すると、鉱山は破壊されます。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:990 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1062
msgid ""
"City center tiles get their terrain's irrigation bonus automatically, if "
"there is no conflicting mine on the tile; however, this does not make cities "
"count as a water source for further irrigation. Irrigation can be built on "
"the city tile simply to allow building further irrigation elsewhere, but "
"will not give the tile any further bonus."
msgstr ""
"都市中心のタイルは、競合する鉱山がない限り、その地形の灌漑ボーナスを自動的に"
"得ます。ただし、これによって都市がさらなる灌漑の水源とみなされることはありま"
"せん。他の場所にさらに灌漑を建設できるようにするためだけに都市のタイルに灌漑"
"を建設することはできますが、タイルにそれ以上のボーナスはありません。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1000 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1072
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1256 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:1286
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:1285 data/alien/terrain.ruleset:830
#: data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1230
msgid "?extra:Mine"
msgstr "鉱山"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1015 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1087
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1275 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1249
msgid ""
"Mines can be built on some types of terrain, which increases the number of "
"production points produced by that tile. Hills get an extra 3 production "
"points per tile; other terrains get 1 extra production point."
msgstr ""
"鉱山は一部の種類の地形に建設でき、そのタイルが産出する生産ポイントを増やしま"
"す。丘ではタイルあたり3、それ以外の地形では1の生産ポイントが追加で得られま"
"す。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1020 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1092
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1280 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:1312
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:1311 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1254
msgid "Building a mine on an irrigated tile will destroy the irrigation."
msgstr "灌漑されたタイルに鉱山を建設すると、灌漑は破壊されます。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1025 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1097
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1313 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:1374
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:1373 data/alien/terrain.ruleset:851
#: data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1287
msgid "?extra:Pollution"
msgstr "汚染"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1043 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1115
msgid ""
"Pollution appears on land tiles around cities with high production or "
"population, or when a Nuclear unit is detonated. It halves all output from "
"its tile, and contributes to the risk of global warming."
msgstr ""
"汚染は生産や人口の多い都市の周辺の陸地タイルに、または核ユニットが爆発したと"
"きに発生します。そのタイルのすべての産出を半分にし、地球温暖化のリスクに寄与"
"します。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1048
msgid ""
"The pollution can only be cleared by dispatching Settlers with the \"clean "
"pollution\" order."
msgstr ""
"汚染は、開拓者を派遣して「汚染除去」命令を与えることでのみ除去できます。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1051
msgid ""
"Pollution from production is likely to start becoming important as your "
"civilization becomes more industrialized, giving you buildings such as "
"Factory and Power Plant which boost production. Replacing a Power Plant with "
"cleaner forms of energy -- a Hydro Plant / Hoover Dam or Nuclear Plant -- "
"will reduce pollution from production, as will a Recycling Center."
msgstr ""
"生産による汚染は、文明が工業化し、工場や火力発電所などの生産を高める都市施設"
"を手に入れるにつれて重要になり始めるでしょう。火力発電所をよりクリーンなエネ"
"ルギー (水力発電所/フーバーダムや原子力発電所) に置き換えると生産による汚染が"
"減り、リサイクル施設でも同様に減ります。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1058 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1130
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1346 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1321
msgid ""
"The city's population starts adding to pollution with the discovery of "
"Industrialization, and Automobile, Mass Production, and Plastics make this "
"worse. Building a Mass Transit in a city eliminates the population's "
"contribution to pollution."
msgstr ""
"都市の人口は工業化の発見とともに汚染に加わり始め、自動車、大量生産、プラス"
"チックによって悪化します。都市に公共交通機関を建設すると、人口による汚染への"
"寄与がなくなります。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1063 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1135
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1351 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:1414
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:1413 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1326
msgid ""
"The contribution of these factors can be seen in the city dialog; once it "
"exceeds a threshold, the excess is the percent chance of pollution appearing "
"each turn."
msgstr ""
"これらの要因の寄与は都市ダイアログで確認できます。それがしきい値を超えると、"
"超過分が毎ターン汚染が発生する確率 (%) になります。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1067 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1139
msgid ""
"When an unused tile becomes polluted, there is the temptation to avoid the "
"effort of cleaning it; but the spread of pollution has far more terrible "
"results than the immediate economic impact -- every polluted tile increases "
"the chance of global warming. Each time global warming advances, the entire "
"world loses coastal land to jungles and swamps, and inland tiles are lost to "
"desert. This tends to devastate cities and leads to global impoverishment."
msgstr ""
"使っていないタイルが汚染されると、除去の手間を省きたくなるものです。しかし、"
"汚染の拡大は目先の経済的影響よりもはるかに恐ろしい結果をもたらします。汚染さ"
"れたタイルはどれも地球温暖化の確率を高めます。地球温暖化が進行するたびに、世"
"界中で海岸沿いの土地がジャングルや湿地に変わり、内陸のタイルは砂漠に変わりま"
"す。これは都市に壊滅的な打撃を与え、世界的な貧困につながりがちです。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1075 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1147
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1363 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:1426
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:1425 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1338
msgid ""
"The risk of global warming is cumulative; the longer polluted tiles are left "
"uncleaned, the higher the risk becomes, and the risk can linger for some "
"time even after all pollution has been cleaned. If a long time passes with "
"an elevated risk of warming, its effects will be all the more severe when it "
"does occur."
msgstr ""
"地球温暖化のリスクは累積します。汚染されたタイルを除去せずに放置する期間が長"
"いほどリスクは高まり、すべての汚染を除去した後もしばらくリスクが残ることがあ"
"ります。温暖化のリスクが高い状態が長く続くと、実際に発生したときの影響はより"
"深刻になります。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1084 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1156
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1372 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:1435
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:1434 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1347
msgid "Minor Tribe Village"
msgstr "先住民の集落"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1103 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1175
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1391 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:1454
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:1453 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1366
msgid ""
"Villages (also called \"huts\") are primitive communities spread across the "
"world at the beginning of the game. Any land unit can enter a village, "
"making the village disappear and deliver a random response. If the village "
"proves hostile, it could produce barbarians or the unit entering may simply "
"be destroyed. If they are friendly, the player could receive gold, a new "
"technology, a military unit (occasionally a settler; and sometimes a unit "
"that the player cannot yet create), or even a new city."
msgstr ""
"村 (「小屋」とも呼ばれます) はゲーム開始時に世界中に点在する原始的な共同体で"
"す。どの陸上ユニットも村に入ることができ、村は消えてランダムな反応が返ってき"
"ます。村が敵対的であれば、蛮族が現れたり、入ったユニットが単に破壊されたりす"
"ることがあります。友好的であれば、プレイヤーは金、新しい科学技術、軍事ユニッ"
"ト (時には開拓者や、プレイヤーがまだ生産できないユニット)、さらには新しい都市"
"を得ることもあります。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1112
msgid "Flying units just fly over the village, leaving it untouched."
msgstr "飛行ユニットは村の上を飛び越えるだけで、村には影響しません。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1117 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1222
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1469 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:1601
#: data/sandbox/units.ruleset:30 data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:1570
#: data/civ2civ3/units.ruleset:30 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1441
msgid "Fortress"
msgstr "要塞"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1142
msgid "Fortresses improve defense for land units outside cities."
msgstr "要塞は都市の外にいる陸上ユニットの防御力を高めます。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1146 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1253
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1501 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:44
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:43 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1473
#, no-c-format
msgid "Diplomatic units get a 25% defense bonus in diplomatic fights."
msgstr "外交ユニットは外交上の戦いで25%の防御ボーナスを得ます。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1174 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1313
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1614 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1586
msgid ""
"Roads allow your land units to move more quickly, and on some terrain, also "
"provide a trade bonus."
msgstr ""
"道路を使うと陸上ユニットは速く移動でき、一部の地形では交易ボーナスも得られま"
"す。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1177 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1316
msgid ""
"Building roads on river tiles requires knowledge of Bridge Building. City "
"center tiles automatically get roads, and are an exception to this "
"requirement."
msgstr ""
"川のタイルに道路を建設するには橋梁建設の知識が必要です。都市中心のタイルは自"
"動的に道路を得るため、この要件の例外となります。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1184 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1323
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1624 data/sandbox/terrain.ruleset:1900
#: data/civ2civ3/terrain.ruleset:1792 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1596
msgid "Railroad"
msgstr "鉄道"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1208 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1347
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1648 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1620
msgid ""
"Once you learn the Railroad technology, you may upgrade your roads to "
"railroads. Units expend no movement points when moving along a railroad; you "
"may ride a railroad indefinitely. (As may your enemies!)"
msgstr ""
"鉄道の科学技術を習得すると、道路を鉄道にアップグレードできます。ユニットは鉄"
"道に沿って移動するときに移動力を消費しません。鉄道ではどこまでも移動できま"
"す。(敵も同様です!)"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1212
msgid ""
"A railroad also increases by half (rounding down) all kinds of resources "
"produced by a tile. A tile whose road is upgraded to a railroad retains any "
"trade bonus from the road as well."
msgstr ""
"鉄道はまた、タイルが産出するあらゆる種類の資源を半分 (端数切り捨て) 増加させ"
"ます。道路を鉄道にアップグレードしたタイルは、道路による交易ボーナスもそのま"
"ま保持します。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1234
msgid "A grassland tile may have a River on it."
msgstr "草原のタイルには川があることがあります。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1236 data/civ2/terrain.ruleset:1383
#: data/classic/terrain.ruleset:1683 data/multiplayer/terrain.ruleset:1655
msgid ""
"Roads and railroads can only be built on River tiles if your civilization "
"has learned Bridge Building technology."
msgstr ""
"川のタイルに道路や鉄道を建設できるのは、文明が橋梁建設の科学技術を習得してい"
"る場合のみです。"

#: data/civ1/terrain.ruleset:1239
msgid ""
"Cities built on or next to rivers are at risk of flooding, which will cause "
"a loss of population and stored food. City Walls eliminate this risk."
msgstr ""
"川の上または隣に建設された都市は洪水の危険があり、人口と蓄えられた食料が失わ"
"れます。城壁はこのリスクをなくします。"

